{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"f4b81f14-63ef-4067-98b7-ea4a6dd351bb","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A definite integral measures accumulated quantity, often shown as area under a curve.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Integral = accumulated area"},{"op":"axes","id":"areaaxes","region":"right","x":{"min":0,"max":4,"label":"x"},"y":{"min":0,"max":5,"label":"y"}}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"f4b81f14-63ef-4067-98b7-ea4a6dd351bb","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Consider the function f of x equals x plus one, from x equals zero to three.","ops":[{"op":"curve","id":"linecurve","axes_id":"areaaxes","expr":"x+1","domain":[0,3]},{"op":"text","id":"interval","anchor":{"el":"areaaxes","side":"below","gap":0.06},"content":"interval: 0 ≤ x ≤ 3"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"What region represents the integral from zero to three?","expected_gist":"the area between the line, the x-axis, and x equals zero and three"}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"f4b81f14-63ef-4067-98b7-ea4a6dd351bb","step":{"id":"s3","script":"The integral adds infinitely thin rectangles, giving the total area beneath the line.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"integral","region":"A2","latex":"\\int_0^3 (x+1)\\,dx"},{"op":"sketch","id":"rectangles","region":"B2","strokes":[[[0.18,0.82],[0.18,0.38],[0.28,0.38],[0.28,0.82]],[[0.28,0.82],[0.28,0.28],[0.38,0.28],[0.38,0.82]],[[0.38,0.82],[0.38,0.18],[0.48,0.18],[0.48,0.82]]]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"f4b81f14-63ef-4067-98b7-ea4a6dd351bb","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Evaluating gives one half times three squared, plus three, so the area is seven and one half.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"answer","region":"A3","latex":"\\int_0^3 (x+1)\\,dx=\\left[\\frac{x^2}{2}+x\\right]_0^3=\\frac{15}{2}"}],"checkpoint":null}}
